WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.763
Unit 3 starts with what
Microsoft gives you.

2
00:00:02.763 --> 00:00:06.449
Each driver family added Entra
modes in specific releases.

3
00:00:06.449 --> 00:00:10.872
Microsoft Data SQL Client added
service principal in two point oh,

4
00:00:10.872 --> 00:00:14.837
managed identity in two point one,
and Default in three point oh.

5
00:00:14.837 --> 00:00:18.998
The O D B C driver added managed
identity in seventeen point three

6
00:00:18.998 --> 00:00:23.313
point one point one and service
principal in seventeen point seven.

7
00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:29.230
The table gives the O L E D B driver eighteen
point three and eighteen point five,

8
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.962
and the J D B C driver twelve point two.

9
00:00:31.962 --> 00:00:35.305
In every family the Entra
password mode is deprecated,

10
00:00:35.305 --> 00:00:37.237
so it's never a migration target.

11
00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:41.777
Microsoft also says a token doesn't
grant database permissions by itself,

12
00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:46.837
and to prefer a specific mode in production,
such as managed identity, over Default.

13
00:00:46.837 --> 00:00:48.957
And on an Arc-enabled Windows server,

14
00:00:48.957 --> 00:00:53.549
a process can get the machine's managed
identity token only if it runs as a local

15
00:00:53.549 --> 00:00:58.220
administrator, or as a member of the
Hybrid Agent Extension Applications group.
